{
  "where_we_lag": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "Pohjanmaa's overlapping crude treatment shares do not lag national values, but public data lack county waiting times and crude MDT recording is low.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "cty:curative:Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
        "cty:life_prolonging:Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
        "cty:symptomatic:Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
        "cty:mdt_recorded:Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
        "bs:coverage:Referral",
        "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "Across overlapping treatment categories, Pohjanmaa's crude curative share is 27.8% (95% CI 23.9–32.2; n=125/449) versus 27.0% (4009/14873) nationally and crude symptomatic share is 36.1% (95% CI 31.8–40.6; n=162/449) versus 39.5% (5871/14873), each 95% confidence interval including the national value, while crude life-prolonging treatment is 43.0% (95% CI 38.5–47.6; n=193/449), whose 95% confidence interval excludes 30.4% (4522/14873) nationally.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:curative:Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:curative",
          "cty:symptomatic:Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:symptomatic",
          "cty:life_prolonging:Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:life_prolonging"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Across overlapping categories, Pohjanmaa's crude share with no treatment record within 12 months—which mixes untreated patients and treatment that was not recorded—is 22.9% (95% CI 19.3–27.1; n=103/449), whose 95% confidence interval excludes and lies below 27.5% (4089/14873) nationally, while crude MDT meeting recording—measuring recording practice, not care—is 6.9% (95% CI 4.9–9.6; n=31/449), whose 95% confidence interval includes 6.0% (893/14873) nationally.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:no_treatment_record:Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:no_treatment_record",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start",
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded",
          "bs:coverage:MDT",
          "q:39e6ba43a9"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Public data do not measure county waiting times for symptoms, primary care, referral, specialist visits, or treatment start, whereas preliminary, unpublished national averages show lung cancer takes 155 days from symptoms to treatment in Finland versus 107 in Sweden and 67 in Denmark, with 56 days patient delay, 41 days in primary care, and 58 days in specialist care.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Symptoms",
          "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health",
          "bs:coverage:Referral",
          "bs:coverage:First_specialist_visit",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start",
          "mot:total_fi",
          "mot:total_se",
          "mot:total_dk",
          "mot:patient",
          "mot:primary",
          "mot:specialist"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "how_sure_are_we": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "Pohjanmaa's crude no-treatment-record share suggests relatively complete treatment recording as an inference, but crude county shares lack age and stage adjustment and public data omit key pathway stages.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "cty:no_treatment_record:Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
        "nat:no_treatment_record",
        "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
        "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "As Pohjanmaa's crude 22.9% (95% CI 19.3–27.1; n=103/449) no-treatment-record share has a 95% confidence interval that excludes and lies below 27.5% (4089/14873) nationally, this is consistent—as an inference, not a finding—with relatively complete treatment recording (so a low curative share is less likely to be only a recording artefact), whereas a journal article's about 90% HILMO match covers diagnoses only.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:no_treatment_record:Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:no_treatment_record",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start",
          "lit:hilmo_90"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The county shares are crude and have separate limitations: (a) they are not age-adjusted (age-adjusted values exist only from Kuva 16 for curative treatment by sex, digitised from a figure at about ±0.5 percentage points, with national reference lines of 26.7% for men and 26.9% for women); (b) they cannot be stage-adjusted because stage at diagnosis is missing for about 48% of patients.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:curative:Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "k16:curative:men:national",
          "k16:curative:women:national",
          "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
          "q:7885b0974f"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In the report, primary care visits are not included in the report's data, occupational health is not mentioned, imaging appears only as clinical diagnosis basis in about 20% of patients (not imaging use or waits), HILMO shows whether a specialist visit occurred within 12 months (93.6%) but not when, and HILMO logs MDT codes only from direct patient contacts.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health",
          "q:323de0d90d",
          "bs:coverage:Imaging",
          "q:5eb155decc",
          "bs:coverage:First_specialist_visit",
          "bs:coverage:MDT",
          "q:39e6ba43a9"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "what_to_do_first": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "The team recommends that Pohjanmaa report THL 21/2016 access times with handover alerts, standardise referrals with a diagnostic contact person, and publish stage, drug, and MDT recording completeness.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "rec:1",
        "rec:2",
        "rec:3"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "Because the Health Care Act sets no legal maximum time for a cancer suspicion and national access-time monitoring is lacking, the team recommends reporting access times from referral to treatment start using THL Ohjaus 21/2016 definitions (for 16 cancers) with handover alerts while the STM roadmap (measure 3.1.2) plans cancer-specific pathways and access times by 2026–2028.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:1",
          "law:no_max",
          "thl:21_2016",
          "q:ccda20dce9",
          "q:24169121a4",
          "q:def306014c",
          "q:b326e35410"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Since mentor insight notes a weak referral gets lower urgency, the team recommends a KYS-style referral template, referring persistent symptoms after a normal X-ray (in KYS's regional pathway document), and a diagnostic contact, while the Filha programme's diagnostics recommendation is to be carried out before the 2030 mid-term evaluation and the STM roadmap plans referral criteria (measure 2.5.2) and coordinator guidance (measure 1.2.3) by 2026–2028.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:2",
          "mentor:kaisa_referral",
          "reg:kys_template",
          "reg:kys_persistent",
          "reg:only_kys_xray",
          "reg:named_contact",
          "q:29b792498e",
          "q:614febebf2",
          "q:c61439b30f",
          "q:fc81032a80",
          "q:050ee09ebe"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Because stage is missing for about 48% of patients and Pohjanmaa's crude MDT-recorded share—measuring recording practice, not care—is 6.9% (95% CI 4.9–9.6; n=31/449, whose 95% confidence interval includes 6.0%, 893/14873 nationally), the team recommends publishing county recording completeness for stage, drug treatment, and MDT coding while the STM roadmap (measure 3.2.1) plans a national quality registry (2026–2028 decree; 90%-coverage reports by 2029–2031).",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:3",
          "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
          "q:7885b0974f",
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded",
          "bs:coverage:MDT",
          "q:950a2f797b",
          "q:82d365cd2c",
          "q:f07a34a300",
          "q:4a856bd695",
          "q:f540c706f8"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
